DAY_DATA = {'day': 158, 'part1_intro': "Day 158 — KnightMotives — modernization requirements — uses the roadmap's case or exam scope as the input. Each topic names the decision boundary, evidence owner and business effect; no product choice or score is treated as a fact without supporting evidence.", 'part2_intro': 'Trace the full reasoning path: supplied fact or requirement, candidate design or study rule, acceptance evidence, failure signal, owner and condition that would change the choice. The topology is a teaching model, not evidence of a live system or exam result.', 'part3_intro': 'These deep-dive cases preserve the original case or exam reasoning while separating supplied facts from architectural inference. The incident diagrams are synthetic exercises, not observed production events.', 'part4_intro': "The labs retain each day's original decision work, expanded into the eight execution stages used on Day 142. Complete them with prior artifacts and synthetic inputs unless an earlier roadmap page explicitly authorizes a cloud test.", 'exit_summary': 'A source-linked dependency map and prioritized business outcomes.', 'arch_table_html': '\n<table><caption>Day-specific architecture and evidence path</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic boundary</th><th>Decision rule</th><th>Acceptance evidence</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Read the official KnightMotives case</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr><tr><td>Identify ordering, dealer, legacy-system, connectivity, AI, privacy and skills constraints</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'arch_diagram': {'type': 'topology', 'title': 'Day 158: KnightMotives — modernization requirements — evidence and decision path', 'desc': 'Three-tier architecture path for KnightMotives — modernization requirements, showing case or exam inputs, requirements and trade-off evidence, then acceptance and ownership controls.', 'caption': 'Scope: a synthetic evidence path for Day 158 covering Read the official KnightMotives case / Identify ordering, dealer, legacy-system, . It shows reasoning boundaries and verification ownership; it does not prove a production deployment, exam result, price, quota, eligibility or customer outcome.', 'width': 1120, 'height': 690, 'layers': [{'name': 'TIER 1 · INPUTS / DEMAND', 'desc': 'case facts, prompts and constraints', 'x': 10, 'y': 55, 'w': 1100, 'h': 92, 'fill': '#0c2033', 'title_color': '#38bdf8', 'opacity': 0.72}, {'name': 'TIER 2 · EVIDENCE / REASONING', 'desc': 'requirements, alternatives and failure checks', 'x': 10, 'y': 185, 'w': 1100, 'h': 210, 'fill': '#241808', 'title_color': '#f59e0b', 'opacity': 0.64}, {'name': 'TIER 3 · GOVERNANCE / ACCEPTANCE', 'desc': 'owners, acceptance and revisit triggers', 'x': 10, 'y': 435, 'w': 1100, 'h': 115, 'fill': '#062316', 'title_color': '#22c55e', 'opacity': 0.68}], 'components': [{'name': 'Case or prompt', 'detail': 'Day 158 supplied scope', 'x': 60, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Prior artifacts', 'detail': 'facts + decisions + errors', 'x': 435, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Changed constraint', 'detail': 'cost / risk / scope', 'x': 810, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Requirements map', 'detail': 'fact to acceptance', 'x': 60, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Option matrix', 'detail': 'choice + alternative', 'x': 435, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Failure rehearsal', 'detail': 'signal + safe response', 'x': 810, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Evidence owner', 'detail': 'source + artifact', 'x': 245, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}, {'name': 'Acceptance gate', 'detail': 'observed / predicted', 'x': 625, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}], 'flows': [{'x1': 185, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 185, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'extract'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 560, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'trace'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 935, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'challenge'}, {'x1': 310, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 435, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'compare'}, {'x1': 685, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 810, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'rehearse'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 750, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'accept'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 370, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'evidence'}, {'x1': 495, 'y1': 490, 'x2': 625, 'y2': 490, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'review'}], 'boundaries': [{'x': 42, 'y': 205, 'w': 1036, 'h': 140, 'color': '#f59e0b', 'label': 'EVIDENCE CHECK'}, {'x': 220, 'y': 442, 'w': 680, 'h': 94, 'color': '#22c55e', 'label': 'DECISION OWNER'}], 'probes': [{'cx': 185, 'cy': 106, 'label': 'PROBE 1 · input classified', 'badge': 'P1', 'color': '#38bdf8'}, {'cx': 560, 'cy': 272, 'label': 'PROBE 2 · trade-off recorded', 'badge': 'P2', 'color': '#f59e0b'}, {'cx': 750, 'cy': 490, 'label': 'PROBE 3 · acceptance result', 'badge': 'P3', 'color': '#22c55e'}]}, 'topics': [{'key': 'topic-01', 'title': 'Read the official KnightMotives case', 'overview': 'KnightMotives is an automotive manufacturer moving toward a complete automotive experience. The case describes declining experience in hybrid and ICE vehicles, an unreliable online ordering flow, dealer tooling gaps, largely on-premises IT, an outdated supply-chain mainframe and ERP, fragmented vehicle codebases, plant and rural connectivity challenges, security history, EU privacy concerns and a five-year transformation.', 'preview': 'Symptom: The transformation proposal moves customer and manufacturing workflows to cloud services but assumes dealers can replace equipment and plants have stable connectivity. Effect: The read the official knightmotives case decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Separate the case’s business outcomes from its technology proposals. The requirements span vehicle UX and connectivity, build-to-order and dealer workflows, hybrid modernization, autonomous-vehicle development and simulation, data monetization, security/incident response, privacy and workforce capability. Draw these as dependent value streams rather than treating “IoT analytics” as the whole problem.</p><table><caption>KnightMotives discovery register</caption><thead><tr><th>Case fact</th><th>Business outcome</th><th>Constraint or dependency</th><th>Question before design</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Online ordering is unreliable and dealers lack useful data</td><td>Reliable build-to-order and dealer/customer transparency</td><td>Legacy order, ERP and dealer workflows</td><td>Which system owns configuration, price, allocation and order status?</td></tr><tr><td>Plants and rural vehicles have connectivity challenges</td><td>Consistent experience and reliable telemetry</td><td>Intermittent links, bandwidth and offline behavior</td><td>What must work locally when the link is absent?</td></tr><tr><td>Data is siloed and security has suffered breaches</td><td>Safe insight and funding for new capability</td><td>Privacy, segmentation, incident response and consent</td><td>Which data may be monetized, for whom and under what policy?</td></tr><tr><td>Autonomous capability will be targeted in favorable regions</td><td>Safe, compliant research and deployment</td><td>Regulatory variation, simulation and model evidence</td><td>What is the release gate from simulation to road testing?</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-049">Topic 049 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_knightmotives_automotive_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 49 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'The transformation proposal moves customer and manufacturing workflows to cloud services but assumes dealers can replace equipment and plants have stable connectivity. Ordering, service and telemetry fail during a link outage and the business cannot explain which side owns a change.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'The design started with destination products instead of dependency and availability boundaries. Preserve explicit local/offline behavior, phase dealer tooling, inventory network capacity, define ownership and reconcile writes before surfacing a status.', 'root': 'The design started with destination products instead of dependency and availability boundaries. Preserve explicit local/offline behavior, phase dealer tooling, inventory network capacity, define ownership and reconcile writes before surfacing a status.', 'fix': 'The design started with destination products instead of dependency and availability boundaries. Preserve explicit local/offline behavior, phase dealer tooling, inventory network capacity, define ownership and reconcile writes before surfacing a status.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'The case does not supply every latency, capacity, regulatory or funding number. Keep these as discovery questions and do not present them as requirements.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Extract KnightMotives facts and dependencies', 'goal': 'Produce a source-linked dependency map and prioritized business-outcome register.', 'expected': 'A source-linked dependency map that makes offline, dealer, legacy, privacy, security and skills constraints visible.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-158-01-extract-knightmotives-facts-and-depe.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-158-01-extract-knightmotives-facts-and-depe.md`. Record Day 158, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_knightmotives_automotive_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Read and cite. Create day-158-knightmotives-facts.md ; cite the official case page for each statement.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** List outcomes. Record customer, dealer, manufacturing, vehicle, safety, data and workforce outcomes without choosing products.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Map dependencies. Connect online ordering, dealer tools, mainframe/ERP, plants, rural vehicles, analytics, simulation, identity and incident response.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Mark boundaries. Label cloud, on-premises, vehicle, plant, dealer, regional regulatory and data-owner boundaries.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Prioritize. Rank outcomes by customer impact, safety, regulatory exposure, dependency and evidence readiness.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Close out. Save the map and unresolved-question list; link both from the exit artifact.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-158-01-extract-knightmotives-facts-and-depe.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'A source-linked dependency map that makes offline, dealer, legacy, privacy, security and skills constraints visible.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If a requirement is actually a proposed solution, move it to the inference column and write the question that would confirm it.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-158-01-extract-knightmotives-facts-and-depe.md'}}, {'key': 'topic-02', 'title': 'Identify ordering, dealer, legacy-system, connectivity, AI, privacy and skills constraints', 'overview': 'The architecture must support adoption as well as technology. Dealer resources, plant operations, vehicle software compatibility, security response, EU privacy and workforce readiness can change the sequence more than a service feature can.', 'preview': 'Symptom: A business unit publishes aggregated driving data to fund the transformation. Effect: The identify ordering, dealer, legacy-system, connectivity, ai, privacy and skills constraints decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Use a bounded context for vehicle and dealer data. Order state needs a clear owner, idempotency and reconciliation. Vehicle and plant paths need a declared offline queue, retry policy and safe local behavior. Data monetization needs classification, consent or lawful-use decisions, de-identification where appropriate, access controls and an exit path when policy changes. AI/simulation work needs separate research, evaluation, safety and production release boundaries.</p><p>Skills and funding are architecture constraints: a design requiring new platform, data, security and embedded expertise on every team is not a five-year plan without an adoption wave. Define a thin first capability, a training/ownership plan, measurable value and a rollback or pause point.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Decision rule</strong><p>Prefer the wave that reduces a declared customer or safety risk while preserving the ability to stop, reconcile and learn. Do not monetize data merely because it exists.</p></div><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-049">Topic 049 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_knightmotives_automotive_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 49 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'A business unit publishes aggregated driving data to fund the transformation. The pipeline cannot show consent, regional handling, deletion, access or breach response. A security incident now affects trust and funding at once.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'Data value was prioritized before classification, purpose, access and response. Create a data product contract, policy gate, regional controls, audit trail, incident playbook and revocation/deletion path. Treat monetization as an opt-in product with a defined owner.', 'root': 'Data value was prioritized before classification, purpose, access and response. Create a data product contract, policy gate, regional controls, audit trail, incident playbook and revocation/deletion path. Treat monetization as an opt-in product with a defined owner.', 'fix': 'Data value was prioritized before classification, purpose, access and response. Create a data product contract, policy gate, regional controls, audit trail, incident playbook and revocation/deletion path. Treat monetization as an opt-in product with a defined owner.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'De-identification is not a universal guarantee. Validate re-identification risk and legal interpretation with the responsible experts.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Turn constraints into a first modernization wave', 'goal': 'Convert the discovery register into an ordered wave with privacy, skills and adoption gates.', 'expected': 'A bounded first wave with explicit data and operational boundaries, adoption owner, pause trigger and residual risk.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-158-02-turn-constraints-into-a-first-modern.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-158-02-turn-constraints-into-a-first-modern.md`. Record Day 158, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_knightmotives_automotive_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Choose a capability. Select ordering, dealer service, plant connectivity, data platform or simulation as the first bounded wave.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Define the boundary. Name source of truth, offline behavior, identities, data class, region and affected teams.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Set gates. Add security, privacy, reliability, adoption, cost and rollback acceptance.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Model a stop. Stop the wave after a link outage, data-policy change, dealer rejection or migration mismatch. Record safe behavior.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Plan enablement. Add training, support, owner and funding assumptions; label all estimates.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Save. Write the prioritized wave and its evidence plan into the exit artifact.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-158-02-turn-constraints-into-a-first-modern.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'A bounded first wave with explicit data and operational boundaries, adoption owner, pause trigger and residual risk.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If the first wave requires every legacy system to change, shrink it until a reversible user or operator outcome is testable.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-158-02-turn-constraints-into-a-first-modern.md'}}]}
